In the video, the average normal stress in rods AB and BC is determined. Which of the following formulas correctly represents the calculation of the average normal stress (\sigma_{ave}) in rod AB?
A. \sigma_{ave} = F_{AB} \cdot A_{AB}
B. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}}{\pi \cdot d_{AB}}
C. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}}{\pi \cdot d_{AB}^2}
D. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB} \cdot d_{AB}}{A_{AB}}
E. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}}{0.5 \cdot \pi \cdot d_{AB}^2}
F. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}^2}{A_{AB}}
G. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}}{d_{AB}}
H. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{A_{AB}}{F_{AB}}
I. \sigma_{ave} = \frac{F_{AB}}{A_{AB}}
J. None of the above
Please ignore the Quiz question in last frame of the video.

